\date{2025-08-12T21:38:26Z}
\title{Polarisation}
\author{vikraman}
\import{base-macros}

\p{
  Let #{\cat{L}} be a model of classical linear logic with orthogonality #{\blank^\bot} with a Lafont exponential (!).
  Let #{\cat{L}^{!}} and #{\cat{L}^{?}} be the categories of (co)algebras for #{!} and #{?}.
}

\p{
  The orthogonality on #{\cat{L}} lifts to an isomorphism #{{\cat{L}^{!}}\op \natiso \cat{L}^{?}},
  and similarly #{{\cat{L}^{?}}\op \natiso \cat{L}^{!}}.
}

\p{
  Composing the continuations self-adjunction with the above isomorphism gives the shift adjunction between the two polarised categories.
}